        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T15:50:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SkFontMgr has `_factory.cpp` in order to facilitate a default SkFontMgr, but there are no `_factory.h` files because the actual `SkFontMgr_New_Foo` are in the `include/ports/SkFontMgr_foo.h` headers. So in theory this should be `SkTypeface_fontations.h`, but Skia wants all the header names to be unique, so that doesn\u0027t work, does it? The other ports get away with it by the public headers being more generic (and possibly less well named), like `include/ports/SkTypeface_win.h` as the public header and `src/ports/SkTypeface_win_dw.h` as the internal header name.\n\nI\u0027d hate to create yet more churn on this CL, but one Chromium starts using this file it will be more difficult to rename. I feel like this public header should get the \"better\" name of `SkTypeface_fontations.h` and maybe the internal one in `src/ports` should be `SkTypeface_fontations_priv.h` or something (I really dislike the `impl` and `priv` things, but visibility in headers is silly).",
      "revId": "94b30c6b37e29d375fe2bd4b8525bb9b082786cc",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
