        "id": 6395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T16:22:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Renamed header containing external Make function to `SkTypeface_fontations.h`, file in `src/ports/` to `SkTypeface_fontations_priv.h`.",
      "parentUuid": "2df534df_8d536d2a",
      "revId": "94b30c6b37e29d375fe2bd4b8525bb9b082786cc",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0724d8a_65f6a17e",
        "filename": "include/ports/SkTypeface_fontations_factory.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T15:50:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d complain about the inconsistency of this name, but we\u0027re already so inconsistent that making it consistent with anything else would be inconsistent at this point. Though generally Skia tries to make all top level functions like this start with `Sk`. Maybe we should use the existing pattern on SkFontMgr (like `SkFontMgr_New_Android`) and name this function `SkTypeface_New_Fontations`. Though maybe breaking with that and being `SkTypeface_Make_Fontations` would be more consistent with the `Make` terminology used in SkTypeface?\n\nSkia started out with `Create` everywhere, but those all returned raw pointers because it was all C++03. To have a different name when updating to smart pointers `Make` was the replacement. But early on some things used `New`. So now there is a mix of `Create`, `Make`, and `New`. An English thesaurus is quite thick.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "94b30c6b37e29d375fe2bd4b8525bb9b082786cc",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
